{"id": "f94b438d-10e3-47c6-a391-2e7ef6bba9c3", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit your SageMaker notebook instances and Studio domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest. The audit is read-only and covers every associated account and the regions that have SageMaker resources. I'll report back with the findings.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_vHicgKN1cK2wK1niMpbIek", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-exposure-encryption-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run a strictly READ-ONLY security audit of Amazon SageMaker notebook instances and SageMaker domains (Studio / SageMaker AI domains, including user profiles and spaces where relevant) for (1) internet exposure and (2) encryption at rest. Do not make any mutating calls.",
  "context": "The user asked: 'Audit our SageMaker notebooks and domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest.' Agent space account is 012345678901_1 in us-east-1, but workloads may live in ANY associated AWS account (use list_associations to find all monitor/source accounts) and in multiple regions. Enumerate regions where SageMaker is used (check all enabled commercial regions, or at least us-east-1 plus any region where list_notebook_instances / list_domains returns results). Produce an answer for every account+region scanned, and explicitly note any account/region you could not access (permission errors).",
  "resources": ["SageMaker notebook instances", "SageMaker domains", "user profiles / spaces", "associated security groups, subnets, VPCs, KMS keys"],
  "criteria": {
    "notebook_instances": "For each: list_notebook_instances then describe_notebook_instance. Internet exposure: DirectInternetAccess (Enabled = exposed/high), SubnetId/VPC presence (no VPC = AWS-managed internet-enabled), security groups with inbound rules open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 (describe_security_groups), whether subnet has route to an IGW (describe_route_tables) / NAT, RootAccess enabled, notebook URL/presigned access constraints if visible. Encryption at rest: KmsKeyId set (customer managed CMK) vs absent (AWS default/none for the ML storage volume); note key details via kms describe_key if present (key state, rotation). Also note IMDSv2 enforcement (InstanceMetadataServiceConfiguration) as secondary finding.",
    "domains": "For each: list_domains then describe_domain (and list_user_profiles / list_spaces if useful). Internet exposure: AppNetworkAccessType (PublicInternetOnly = exposed/high vs VpcOnly), SubnetIds, VPC, SecurityGroupIds / security group rules open to 0.0.0.0/0, NAT/IGW routing, AuthMode, DomainSettings (e.g. SecurityGroupIds, RStudio), default user/space settings. Encryption at rest: KmsKeyId (EFS volume encryption) - HomeEfsFileSystem KMS key; if absent, flag as using AWS-managed key. Also check S3 output/shared-space artifacts encryption if configured (SharingSettings S3OutputPath/ S3KmsKeyId).",
    "severity": "Rate each finding Critical/High/Medium/Low/Info with a one-line reason and a concise remediation (note that recreate may be required for KMS on existing notebooks/domains).",
    "output_format": "Concise report: (a) scope scanned (accounts/regions, counts of notebooks and domains), (b) a table of resources with columns: account, region, name, direct/public internet access, VPC-only?, open SGs, encryption key (CMK/AWS-managed/none), severity; (c) top findings ranked; (d) any gaps/errors. Keep it shallow-but-complete — enumerate everything, do not hypothesize root causes."
  }
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebooks and domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

